implementationPlan.description:
runSeatJob composition in scripts/local-runner/agent-seat.mjs.
FILE NOTE: agent-seat.mjs and scripts/tests/local-runner-seat.test.mjs are CREATED BY CQ-M07i (task-18809c69, a dependsOn). They are listed as newFiles only because they did not exist when this plan was written; by the time this row is claimable they exist. EDIT them, never recreate or overwrite M07i's content.
Rails: never fall back to running the agent CLI on the host; no seat runs Multipass, and tests use fakes. Read mem:gotcha-local-runner-tests first.
export runSeatJob(input, steps = {}).
input is exactly { project, owner, instance, binding, checkout, commit, cli, credential, onOutput, signal?, timeoutMs? }. Validate every field before any call, else SEAT_JOB_INPUT_INVALID:
- project and checkout: absolute;
- owner: validSeatOwner;
- instance: isOwnedInstanceName;
- binding: { role 'worker'|'qa', workerId, taskId, attemptId, generation }, whose shape scopeRequest validates;
- commit: a full 40- or 64-hex id;
- cli: 'claude' or 'codex';
- credential: { name, value } with exact keys;
- onOutput: a function.
The credential is copied once into the job object and nowhere else.
steps holds the injectable defaults:
- sweep = endAgentJobs;
- reset = resetWorkspace (CQ-M07f: { name, provider, timeoutMs }, resolving 'reset');
- exportSnapshot = exportSourceSnapshot;
- materialize = materializeSnapshot;
- job = runAgentJob;
- importCandidate;
- admit = admitCandidate;
- stop = stopSeat (CQ-M07i);
- forward = seatForward(project) (CQ-M07j1: forward(tool, args, { signal }) resolves the daemon's raw MCP result).
provider = { executable: platformFor(process.platform).executable }. git = exportGit(checkout), resolved once for export and admission.
Order, one fixed code per stage, a stage's own fixed code passing through when it matches /^[A-Z][A-Z0-9_]{0,63}$/:
(1) sweep(instance, provider) must resolve { verified: true }, else SEAT_JOB_SWEEP_UNVERIFIED.
(2) reset({ name: instance, provider }): failure is SEAT_JOB_RESET_FAILED.
(3) exportSnapshot({ repoDir: checkout, commit, git }), then REPLACE its overlay with validateImport([]) (source-snapshot.mjs). The guest workspace is then exactly the commit's tree. The checkout's dirty bytes are peers' or pre-existing, never this VM job's: under verified-local all task work happens in the VM and lands as admitted trees. Failure is SEAT_JOB_EXPORT_FAILED.
(4) materialize({ name: instance, snapshot, provider }): SEAT_JOB_MATERIALIZE_FAILED.
(5) job({ name: instance, binding, job: { cli, credential }, daemonInfoPath: path.join(project, '.moe', 'daemon.json'), forward, onOutput, onObservation, signal, provider, timeoutMs }). A rejection, or failure !== null, is SEAT_JOB_SESSION_FAILED. The observation's exit code is data, reported, never a failure.
(6) importCandidate({ name: instance, provider }): SEAT_JOB_IMPORT_FAILED.
(7) A qa binding with candidate.entries.length > 0 is SEAT_JOB_QA_CANDIDATE_REFUSED: nothing is admitted or applied. A qa binding with an empty candidate skips admission.
(8) worker: admit({ repoDir: checkout, git, baseTree: snapshot.tree, candidate }): SEAT_JOB_ADMISSION_FAILED. admitCandidate writes only git objects through its private index, never the checkout's working tree or index.
Landing hand-off, decided: runSeatJob NEVER writes the task checkout. It resolves a frozen { ok: true, role, commit, baseTree, tree, digest, paths: candidate entries as { path, kind } (no bytes), exitCode, signal, lease, executionReady: false }. CQ-M07m/n land that exact admitted tree on `commit` through the wrapper's existing candidate path (record_candidate treeSha on baseRevision, CQ-V07/V08 delivery). Writing guest paths into a shared checkout would collide with peers' bytes and attribution holds.
The seat VM is stopped (stop({ project, owner, instance })) ONLY on unverified state:
- the sweep is unverified;
- reset failed;
- or the job resolved terminationVerified false.
Every other failure keeps it, because the next job's sweep and reset re-verify it. A failure resolves a frozen { ok: false, code, vm: 'kept'|'stopped'|'stop-failed' }; no stage after a failure runs. The host never spawns the agent CLI.

Rows for runSeatJob in scripts/tests/local-runner-seat.test.mjs (created by CQ-M07i and already in CI; edit it, never recreate it). Prefix SJ; grep first that it is unused.
- SJ1 (DoD 1). The checkout is a temp git repo with one committed file a.txt plus an uncommitted dirty b.txt, using the REAL exportSourceSnapshot and the REAL admitCandidate. VM-side stages are fakes: each has its own provider-level rows in the R-series (endAgentJobs, resetWorkspace, materializeSnapshot, runAgentJob, importCandidate).
  - The fake materialize asserts the overlay is empty, so b.txt never reaches the guest.
  - The fake job returns { failure: null, terminationVerified: true, observation: { kind: 'observation', type: 'exit', code: 0, signal: null }, lease: 'released' }.
  - The fake importCandidate returns validateImport([{ kind: 'file', path: 'a.txt', executable: false, data: <new bytes> }]).
  Result: ok, and `git ls-tree -r <tree>` differs from the commit's tree in exactly a.txt's blob. The checkout's `git status --porcelain=v1 -z`, its index bytes and every file's bytes are identical before and after.
- SJ2 (DoD 2). A canary credential value travels only in the job step's job.credential. A deep scan of every other step's arguments finds it absent: sweep, reset, export, materialize, import, admit, stop, every provider object and forward's calls. It is also absent from process.env (unchanged), the resolved outcome, and every onOutput or stderr write.
- SJ3 (DoD 3). A qa binding with a one-entry candidate gives SEAT_JOB_QA_CANDIDATE_REFUSED; admit is never called and the checkout is unchanged. A qa binding with an empty candidate gives ok with no admit call.
- SJ4 (DoD 4, table). Failing each stage in turn gives its fixed code, with no later stage called and no admit call:
  - sweep unverified: vm 'stopped';
  - reset throws: 'stopped';
  - export throws: 'kept';
  - materialize throws: 'kept';
  - the job rejects or returns failure non-null: 'kept'; with terminationVerified false: 'stopped';
  - import throws: 'kept';
  - admission throws: 'kept'.
  Also: a stop that throws gives 'stop-failed'; invalid input gives SEAT_JOB_INPUT_INVALID with every step untouched. The checkout stays byte-identical in every row.
